<title>FRANCE: French consumer prices rose final 0.2 pct in Dec.</title>
<headline>French consumer prices rose final 0.2 pct in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following final data. It said on Jan 10 that prices in December rose 0.2 percent from the previous month, giving a year-on-year rise of 1.7 percent.</p>
<p>					 Dec	Nov	Dec 1995</p>
<p>    Month-on-month inflation   0.2     -0.1	  0.1</p>
<p>    Year-on-year inflation     1.7	1.6	  2.1</p>
<p>    CPI Index (base 1990)    114.4	114.2	112.5</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990.</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.17    107.4   0.4    0.9    1.3</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  33.05    108.6   0.1   -0.2    0.5</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.76    125.2   0.1    0.0    1.9</p>
<p> Energy				8.25    114.9   0.3    2.3    6.6</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.58    127.7   1.2    0.7    2.0</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.55    129.6   0.1    0.1    2.2</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.64    110.2   0.1    0.2    1.1</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.06    113.4   0.1    0.3    1.5</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
